## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
ASX operates as a fab-lite company, relying on foundries like TSMC and Samsung for production. Its customer concentration in AI and HPC markets creates exposure to cyclicality in data center demand. While the company benefits from secular growth in AI, its dependency on external fabs introduces execution risk during inventory digestion phases.  

**Severity:** **MEDIUM** (high customer concentration in volatile end-markets).  

